{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CediSLUn8feJp6ssbTtYY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VERDICT: pass\nCONSENSUS_BLOCKING: no\nRATIONALE: There is no Mercury answer to defend or attack — Mercury remained HTTP 402 absent, and per the operator's standing rule that absence caps and continues rather than blocks. Reviewing the host-attested receipts directly: all five attack questions are answered by code at HEAD. (1) `_normalizeHydrationCandle` runs both `t` and `etime` through `ohlcTimestampMs` (run-empire-v2.js:1613-1616), with a finite-check on `t` and a `?? (t + timeframeMs)` fallback for `etime`, so `latest.etime || latest.t` at 1748 and 2906 is milliseconds — corroborated by both call-site excerpts. (2) The three production call sites (939, 1748, 2906) are all visible inside attested excerpts; the \"no other calls anywhere\" totality rests on the EVIDENCE.md AST claim, which is TESTIMONY about a host probe, but no receipt contradicts it and the three visible sites match it exactly. (3) The producer conversion is one added line plus captured boolean — the StateManager monotonic gate, its rejection semantics, and all fallbacks are unchanged; this is minimum Fourth Shape producer surgery. (4) Trace categories are literal booleans and the writer's actual return; the handler's invalid-timestamp/missing-symbol returns (910-922) precede both the mark and the trace. (5) `handleMarketData` is only invoked under `if (tf === activeTf)` (excerpt 963-982). Two mechanical nits noted below; neither is blocking and neither can be raised past MECHANICAL on this evidence.\nDISAGREEMENT: EVIDENCE.md claims `mark_rejected` is reachable only \"for a valid but genuinely stale timestamp.\" That is incomplete: `updateLastPrice` also returns false for `!(price > 0)` or non-number price (core/StateManager.js:899), and the handler does not gate `ohlcData[5]` positivity before the call, so a zero/negative/NaN close would also be labeled `mark_rejected`. The label is still truthful (writer rejected), but the evidence doc's reachability claim overstates exclusivity. MECHANICAL, RECEIPT-based. Second nit: the ms→s→ms round trip (`normalizeOhlcForProcessor` divides `etimeMs/1000` at :531, handler re-multiplies via `toTimestampMs` truncation at :62) can lose 1ms to float truncation on non-second-aligned etimes, allowing a spurious equal-time rejection edge; negligible impact, MECHANICAL.\nREQUIRED_RECHECK: none\nRECHECK_PROMPT: none\nNEXT_CHECK: Host-attested transcript of `grep -rn \"updateLastPrice\" --include=\"*.js\" .` at HEAD (or re-run of the Acorn scan with the command and raw output captured in the run ledger, not summarized into EVIDENCE.md) — this converts the AST totality claim from TESTIMONY to RECEIPT.\nCANDIDATE SET: examined 11 of 11 supplied excerpts, covering 7 files, against a touched-file count of 3 (run-empire-v2.js, test/aggregate-source-backfill.test.js, CHANGELOG.md). Candidates: run-empire-v2.js:465-532 (converter identity), :905-982 (handler), :1601-1629 (_normalizeHydrationCandle), :1654-1750 (boot hydration), :2821-2908 (liveness backfill); core/StateManager.js:892-920 (writer/reader); core/CandleProcessor.js:500-512 (ms tripwire); foundation/ohlc-normalize.js:35-62 (toTimestampMs); test/aggregate-source-backfill.test.js:21-78; CHANGELOG.md:8-15; EVIDENCE.md:1-204 (probe outputs, AST scans, prior run history). Prior-fix ledger entries (ALPACA-FLIP, CONFIG-LOADER-CRASH, MATRIX-SWEEP) reviewed for overlap: none touch updateLastPrice paths.\nAST EVIDENCE: No AST tooling available in this Fable pass (named absence). Relied on: EVIDENCE.md's two Acorn scans (155-file runtime set; 635-file full tracked universe, 631 strict + 4 acorn-loose, refs at StateManager.js:898 method + run-empire-v2.js 936/939, 1747/1748, 2905/2906) — TESTIMONY; corroborated by direct line-visibility of all three call sites inside independently hashed excerpts — RECEIPT. The touched config key `dataFeed.bootRestHydrationLimit` / `livenessBackfillLimit` / `maxBackfillAgeMultiplier` / `maxBackfillAgeSlackMs` reads have no AST scan cited — named absence, pre-existing code, out of diff scope.\nINHERITED: run-empire-v2.js — `v: Number(raw?.v ?? raw?.volume ?? 0)` silent 0 volume default (:1626); `etime` silent synthesis `t + timeframeMs` when broker omits etime (:1616); `latest.etime || latest.t` ||-pattern on trading timestamps at 1748/2906 (0 unreachable but pattern inherited); console.warn-and-continue on unnormalizable/invalid payloads (:907, :912) — swallowed drops; `Number.isFinite(latest.v) ? latest.v : null` null default. core/StateManager.js — `getLastPrice` returns `get(symbol) || null` (:919), a price-0-falsy || on trading data. All inherited, all unfixed, none touched by this diff. CHANGELOG.md, test file — none.\nFOURTH SHAPE CLASSIFIER: classified 4 of 4 gates in scope. (1) Producer conversion `ohlcTimestampMs(ohlcData[1])` — producer-fixable, and it IS the producer fix, correctly placed. (2) `canUpdateLastPrice` writer-availability guard — true boundary (pre-existing guard, refactored to captured boolean, no behavior change). (3) StateManager monotonic rejection — true boundary tripwire, deliberately unchanged. (4) CandleProcessor ms throw (:500-512) — true boundary, unchanged, independently corroborates REST candle ms units.\nALLEGATIONS: A1 — `mark_rejected` reachability overstated in EVIDENCE.md (invalid-price path also yields it): MECHANICAL, RECEIPT. A2 — 1ms float-truncation drift on ms→s→ms round trip enabling edge equal-time rejection: MECHANICAL, RECEIPT. A3 — AST totality (no fourth caller repo-wide) rests on doc-embedded probe output: MECHANICAL, TESTIMONY. A4 — `CANDLE_NORMALIZED` emits `etime` in seconds (:929) while `LAST_PRICE_INFLUENCE` emits `eventTime` in ms in the same handler, a unit-inconsistency footgun for trace consumers: MECHANICAL, RECEIPT, pre-existing/out-of-diff. No SUBSTANTIVE allegation.\nSUBSTANTIVE RESOLUTION: none — no substantive finding exists; Mercury seat absent (402), Kimi seat not present in this pass, so no seat disagreement to escalate.\nWHAT I EXAMINED: All 11 host-attested excerpts and their manifest hashes; the pre-change handler receipt quoted in EVIDENCE.md; the trusted-host StateManager probe output; both AST scan summaries; the four prior adversarial run dispositions; the focused test assertions; the prior-fixes ledger matches.\nDID NOT EXAMINE: Any repo file outside the attested excerpts (no repo tools this pass); the raw AST scan command/output transcript; the actual git diff against predecessor 4878c01 (SHA claimed, not shown); handler body beyond line 982 (excerpt boundary — active-branch content after `handleMarketData` unverified except via the source-string test); definitions of NUMERIC_EPOCH_STRING_RE / NUMERIC_LIKE_STRING_RE (above the ohlc-normalize excerpt); `candleToProcessorOhlc`, `_getRestRecoveryScopeEnvelope`, `normalizeOhlc` internals; Jest run output (test pass status is testimony).\nASSUMED: The host-attested manifest hashes genuinely bind excerpts to HEAD artifacts; the EVIDENCE.md-embedded probe and AST outputs were produced on the trusted host as claimed; the three-file diff scope claim is accurate (no fourth file touched); ohlcData[1] entering the handler is always a positive finite seconds value per normalizeOhlcForProcessor's gate; sandbox run_check carries no authority (none was relied upon)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":40094,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":40094},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[REDACTED]","uuid":"[REDACTED]","timestamp":"2026-09-02T01:07:28.994Z","request_id":"req_011CediSHYfguPDuo5SiPg5q"}
